  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing Development Gaps in Communities of Origin of Migrants in Nicaragua</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nicaragua has been a country of origin and transit of migrants. In recent years, Nicaraguan migratory flows have increased, with main destination countries being the United States of America, Costa Rica, Spain, and Panama. The socioeconomic situation and social exclusion are factors that drive migration. In this context, this initiative seeks to contribute to the reduction of the main development gaps of the communities of origin in the North and West areas of the dry corridor in Nicaragua. To achieve this, IOM will implement three actions: the first action will contribute to understand the developmental gaps in communities of origin of migrants through a study based on the Monitoring Matrix, the development of an analytical agenda for the identification of the main Human Mobility (DTM). The second action consists in the formulation of a multisectoral strategy to reduce the main developmental gaps in communities of origin of migrants. The third action is oriented towards the development of skills and abilities in the management of communication technologies and digital networks for adolescents and young entrepreneurs in vulnerable conditions.</narrative>
  </description>
